dinov3 is the cloned official repository of DINOv3.
We use the ViT-L version of DINOv3.

train_dino_classifier.py:
trains a DINO classifier on the cropped frames, given a chosen split.

train_dino_mil.py:
trains a DINO MIL model (binary) on the cropped informative clips, given a chosen split. Can also use the classifier
weights produced in train_dino_classifier (--classifier_checkpoint).

utils.py:
some utils mostly specific to DINO

train_dino_transformer.py:
trains the transformer aggregator (DinoSelfAttention, head shared with convnext/ via transformer/model.py) over
32-frame bags; --cluster_sample samples one frame per k-means cluster (clustering/, Paxos2025 only). Saves
architecture_config.json next to the checkpoint; load runs with DinoSelfAttention.from_checkpoint(run_dir).

hp_sweep.py:
grid search over transformer HPs on split_1 (results: hp_sweep_results_merged.csv). Trial args come from
train_dino_transformer.build_parser(), so new training args are picked up automatically.

vis_attention.py / vis_video_results.py / vis_classifier_attention.py:
attention plots per video / per-video prediction CSVs for several models / occlusion heatmaps for the frame
classifier (5-class checkpoints are scored by P(grade >= 2)).

Removed experiments (see git history):
- train_dino_transformer_rope.py (RoPE on each frame's position in the original video): 5-class, 5 splits
  (runs/dino_sa_all_split_*_1005_1239_rope_1000.0_300): best QWK 0.843 / 0.807 / 0.839 / 0.725 / 0.775
  (mean ~0.80); abandoned. Needed frame_maps/ JSONs that no pipeline step writes.
- train_dino_transformer_alt_sampling.py (hierarchical: 32 anchor frames x 16-frame regions, local + global
  attention): one run (runs/dino_hier_anchor32x16_all_split_1_0929_2004_full) never finished an epoch, no results.
- vis_mil_results.py, full_evaluation.py: superseded by vis_video_results.py. Last 4-way eval of the MIL model
  (max-attention frame / uniform 32 / all frames / 10x ensemble), kept for reference:

